		"note": "How the flame's light is made of what is in it (Stage 82). Calibrated, not measured, but where stated: per_mol, the light of a mole of sodium in the flame at its 1927 C (the lab burner's) as the sum of its lines, in multiples of the room's light at 560 nm times nanometres, per pixel of path (a drop of 0.1 M, 2 umol, then outshines the flame's own blue as a sodium flame does); every element's atoms by the same Boltzmann sum over their lines (g_k A_ki exp(-hc E_k/kT) / lambda over the ground level's g, the partition function taken as it: measured lines, an approximated partition); band_share, the share of an element's light its molecule's bands carry (the alkaline earths' and copper's flames are their monohydroxides' colours: Gaydon, Meyerriecks and Kosanke); band_fwhm_nm, a band's width (their spectra's, a few nm); fade_s, how long a drop's metal lasts in the flame (the 1/e time of a loop's few seconds); drop_ml, what a loop carries.",
